## usage
$ resid-cmw
usage: resid-cmw <command> [args]

  inspect <cmw> [--values]                 tree of records and collections
  diag <cmw>                               CBOR diagnostic notation
  check <cmw>...                           validate; exit 1 if any is not a CMW
  wrap <media-type> <file> [--ind I] -o <out>
                                           a record carrying the file's bytes
  collect [--type T] <label>=<cmw>... -o <out>
                                           a collection of existing CMWs
  extract <cmw> <path> [--value] [-o <out>]
                                           the CMW at path (--value: a record's bytes)
  set <cmw> <path> <member-cmw> -o <out>   add or replace the member at path
  remove <cmw> <path> -o <out>             remove the member at path

A path is labels joined by "/" ("" or "/" is the root). <out> may be "-"
for stdout. An indicator is a number or names joined by ",":
  reference-values, endorsements, evidence, attestation-results

[exit 2]
